speechtext:
On the order:	Government notices of
motion:
1.	That a select committee be appointed to consider the policy, operations and expenditures of the national research council, Atomic Energy of Canada Limited and Eldorado Mining and Refining Limited, and to report from time to time their observations and opinions thereon;
2.	That notwithstanding standing order No. 67, the committee shall consist of 20 members, of which 11 shall be a quorum;
3.	That the committee be empowered to sit during the sittings of the house, to print such papers and evidence from day to day as may be ordered by the committee and to send for persons, papers and records.

Mr. Speaker, the answer to parts 1 and 2 of this question is that communications were received by the Minister of Transport from organizations and municipal authorities

as listed below, and that all members of parliament in the area have shown a continuing interest in the matter:
United Markham and Vaughan ratepayers association, August 20, 1959;
Township of Vaughan, resolution undated;
Township of Pickering, August 12, 1959;
Township of Markham, April 9, 1959;
Committee representing East Vaughan central ratepayers, August 6, 1959;
Southwest Pickering ratepayers association, April 21, April 29 and July 3, 1959.
The answer to part 3 is: the township of Vaughan and the committee representing East Vaughan central ratepayers.
